    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d53">

                <pb facs="0099" n="89" xml:id="pg89"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/4–945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-09T16:00:00+07:00">April 9, 1945—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 9—8:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>601. In view of developing Japanese threat to Sian, HQ United States Army [at]
                    Chungking has offered, if and when it becomes advisable to effect a general
                    withdrawal from Sian, to evacuate American civilians on its returning troop
                    transport planes. Embassy Secretary at Sian has been so informed and has been
                    authorized to discuss matter with American Army authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
